cture of values: Theoretical advances and empirical tests in 20 countries. Adv Exp Soc Psychol. 1992;25:1–65. [ Google Scholar ] Arciniega LM, González L, Soares V, Ciulli S, Giannini M. Cross-cultural validation of the work values scale evat using multi-group confirmatory factor analysis and confirmatory multidimensional scaling. Spanish J Psychol. 2009;12:767–772. doi: 10.1017/S1138741600002134. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Arciniega L, González L. Desarrollo y validación de la escala de valores hacia el trabajo EVAT 30. Rev Psicol Soc. 2000;15:281–296. doi: 10.1174/021347400760259712. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Altamirano Bustamante E, Altamirano Bustamante M, Altamirano Bustamante N. In: Ética Clínica una perspective transfuncional. Altamirano Bustamante M, Garduño Espinosa J, García Peña MC, Muñoz Hernández O, editor. México: Corinter; 2006. pp. 135–170. [ Google Scholar ] Marshall MN. Sampling for qualitative research. Fam Pract. 1996;13(6):522–526. doi: 10.1093/fampra/13.6.522. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Mason M. Sample Size and Saturation in PhD Studies Using Qualitative Interviews. Qual Soc Res. 2010;11:Art 8. [ Google Scholar ] Little M, Gordon J, Markham P, Rychetnik L, Kerridge I. Virtuous acts as practical medical ethics: an empirical study. J Eval Clin Pract. 2011;17:948–953. doi: 10.1111/j.1365-2753.2011.01730.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Laín Entralgo P. La relación médico-enfermo. Madrid: Alianza; 1983. [ Google Scholar ] Olson EJ, Drage LA, Auger RR. Sleep deprivation, physician performance, and patient safety. Chest. 2009;136:1389–1396. doi: 10.1378/chest.08-1952. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Shanafelt TD, Balch CM, Bechamps G, Russell T, Dyrbye L, Satele D, Collicott P, Novotny P, Sloan J, Freischlag J. Burnout and medical errors among American surgeons. Ann Surg. 2010;251:995–1000. doi: 10.1097/SLA.0b013e3181bfdab3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Anderson E. Value in Ethics and Economics. Cambridge