Personal licenses and training: engineers-Information about license types and applications. https://www.caa.co.uk/default.aspx?catid=177 (accessed 18 Feb 2018). 28. Baker A, Groom M. Naval Air Operations : Rainford DJ, Gradwell DP, Ernsting’s Aviation Medicine 2006. Chapter 35: 539-544 London, UK: Fourth Ed Edward Arnold Publishers, 2006. [ Google Scholar ] 29. Weeks SR, McAuliffe CL, DuRussel D, et al. Physiological and psychological fatigue in extreme conditions: the military example physical medicine and rehabilitation. Pm R 2010;5:438–41. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Pavitt AJ, Pavitt CW, Harron K, et al. The clinical, occupational and financial outcomes associated with a bespoke specialist clinic for military aircrew-a cohort study. QJM 2016;109:309–17. 10.1093/qjmed/hcv184 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. EU 290/2012, Article 1 (2)(12) http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?qid=1473408020778&uri=CELEX:32012R0290 (accessed 7 May 2018). 32. Military Aviation Authority. MAA02: military aviation authority master glossary. https://www.gov.uk/government/uploads/systemuploads/attachment_data/file/456610/MAA02_Issue_6.1.pdf . 33. European Air Safety Agency. Annex VII the draft Commission Regulation on ‘Air Operations — OPS’ Part-NCO — IR. https://www.easa.europa.eu/system/files/dfu/Part-NCO_IR.pdf (accessed 18 Feb 2018). 34. Federal Aviation Administration FAA. Acceleration in aviation: G-Force. 2015. 35. Fischer U. Der Kreislaf unter Beschleunigung. Roentgenaufnahmen beim Affen. Luftfahtmedizin 1937;2:1–13. [ Google Scholar ] 36. Mitchell SJ, Evans AD. Flight safety and medical incapacitation risk of airline pilots. Aviat Space Environ Med 2004;75:260–8. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Pedersen CT, Kay GN, Kalman J, et al. EHRA/HRS/APHRS expert consensus on ventricular arrhythmias. Europace 2014;16:1257–83. 10.1093/europace/euu194 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Parsons I, Pavitt C, Chamley R, et al. CT c